# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

## Summary
Successfully implemented Vercel Speed Insights for this Django project using the CDN-based vanilla JavaScript approach.

## What Was Done

### 1. Documentation Research
- Fetched the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
- Identified the appropriate installation method for Django projects (CDN-based script injection)
- Found implementation examples from GitHub to confirm the approach

### 2. Implementation Approach
Since this is a Django project without npm/Node.js, I used the CDN-based vanilla JavaScript method:
- Uses ES6 module imports from jsDelivr CDN
- Imports the `injectSpeedInsights` function from `@vercel/speed-insights@1`
- Script is injected in the `<head>` section of each HTML template

### 3. Files Modified

Modified 6 HTML templates to include Speed Insights:

1. **planner/templates/auth_base.html** - Base template for authentication pages (login, register)
2. **planner/templates/home.html** - Landing/home page template
3. **planner/templates/create_trip.html** - Trip creation page
4. **planner/templates/expense.html** - Expense tracking page
5. **planner/templates/history.html** - History page
6. **planner/templates/trip.html** - Trip planner page

### 4. Code Added
Each template now includes the following script in the `<head>` section:

```html
<!-- Vercel Speed Insights -->
<script type="module">
  import { injectSpeedInsights } from 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@vercel/speed-insights@1/dist/index.mjs';
  injectSpeedInsights();
</script>
```

## Implementation Details

- **No package.json needed**: Since this is a Django project, we don't need to install npm packages
- **CDN-based approach**: Uses jsDelivr CDN to load the Speed Insights library
- **Automatic tracking**: The script will automatically track Core Web Vitals and performance metrics
- **Production-only**: Speed Insights only tracks data in production/preview environments on Vercel
- **Template coverage**: All main user-facing templates now include Speed Insights
- **Child templates**: Templates that extend `auth_base.html` (login.html, register.html) automatically inherit Speed Insights

## Verification

Verified implementation by:
- Checking that the script was successfully added to all 6 templates
- Confirming proper HTML syntax and placement (in `<head>` after fonts, before styles)
- Ensuring consistent indentation and formatting across all templates

## Next Steps

When deployed to Vercel:
1. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel Dashboard for this project
2. Deploy the application to Vercel (production or preview)
3. Speed Insights will automatically begin collecting performance metrics
4. View metrics in the Vercel Dashboard under the Speed Insights tab

## Notes

- Speed Insights will NOT track data in local development
- Data collection only happens on Vercel deployments
- The CDN approach is ideal for projects without a build system
- Uses latest version (@1) which will receive automatic updates for patches
